        "message": "Document how to actually run and use Bullet.\n\nThe README opened on a source build and a simulator demo, which answers\n\"how do I prove this checkout\" and not \"how do I use this\". Someone who\nruns `bullet tui` first had no way to learn what the panes are, which keys\ndo anything, or why the screen is empty.\n\nAdds an operator tutorial: prerequisites, starting the console,\nauthenticating without putting a token in argv, the full TUI keymap, what\neach view reads, the web Portal, and how to seed a ledger so the views are\nnot empty.\n\nIt also states plainly what does not work yet - submissions are accepted\nand then settle UNKNOWN, and neither surface can approve, retry or cancel\n- and carries a troubleshooting table for the refusals a first run\nactually produces.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>",
